cate the position.\n3.  **N: b1-c3**: A solid developing move that controls the center, but less urgent than securing the King.\n\nReason: Given the open center and material lead, the priority is to deny Black any tactical chances against the White King. Castling achieves this efficiently while simultaneously improving the activity of the Rooks. It consolidates the advantage and prepares for a safe middlegame attack.\n\nAnswer: K: e1-g1"}
