. I capture the Black Knight (winning material).\n2. My Knight on f7 attacks the Black Queen (d8) and Rook (h8) simultaneously (Royal Fork).\n3. The Black King CANNOT recapture the Knight because f7 is protected by my Queen, and a King cannot move into check.\n4. Black will be forced to move the Queen, allowing me to capture the Rook on h8 next, or lose the Queen.\nThis sequence wins at least a Knight and a Rook for free.\n\nReason: The move N: e5-f7 is a tactical strike that wins a piece immediately and sets up a winning fork on the King and Queen/Rook. Since the capture is supported by the Queen, the Black King cannot retake, leading to a decisive material advantage.\n\nAnswer: N: e5-f7'}
